# Project Rules & Model Selection Guidelines

## Model Selection Rule
At the start of every task, the AI agent must explicitly ask:
**"Which model for this — Flash or Pro+Claude?"**
- Never assume.
- Use Gemini Flash for all routine tasks.
- Use Pro/Claude only for complex logic, security, and payments.

## Codebase Modification Rules
- Never rewrite entire files — only edit specific lines using targeted replacement.
- Before starting any task — confirm the file exists and check if the feature is already built.
- Never rebuild working features.
- Skip "shall I proceed?" — output/execute direct code only.
- Batch related small changes into one single task.
- Never re-read files already present in context.
- Check for existing similar components before creating new ones.
